  "body": "The quick tier picks test binaries from each suite's `Gate map` header. 86 suites in `crates/app/tests` still name a module as `app::<module>` although M4.1 moved it to its own crate, so a change under `crates/post/src/post/` selects 3 of the 28 suites that name `app::post` (found by the #919 research). `heidenhain_cycles` has no map at all. A fix that touches only a moved module can pass the quick gate without its pinning suites running.\n\nThe diff is xtask and test headers only, but this is the gate that guards posted G-code: check the selection with unit tests, not by eye.\n\nDone means: no suite names a moved module as `app::<module>`; `heidenhain_cycles` has a map; an xtask unit test pins that a change under `crates/post/src/post/` selects the post dialect suites, and the same for one sim and one motion module.\n\nLists, counts and evidence: the research comment on #919 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/919#issuecomment-6808141599).\n\nPart of #919.\n",
